          "correctOptionId": "4",
          "marks": 1,
          "negativeMarks": 0.25,
          "explanation": "<p>Ten persons: B, F, H, J, M, P, S, U, W and Z</p>\n\n<p>i) M sits third to the right of H.</p>\n\n<p>ii) Z is an immediate neighbor of both M and U.</p>\n\n<p>iii) P sits immediate right of U.&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"//storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/21/02/F1_Shabarish_Shraddha_19.02.2021_D1.png\" /></p>\n\n<p>iv) S is not a neighbor of H and sits third to the right of W.</p>\n\n<p>v) B is not a neighbor of W and P.</p>\n\n<p>vi) Number of persons between J and H is same as number of persons between Z and J.</p>\n\n<p>So, the final arrangement is,</p>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"//storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/21/02/F1_Shabarish_Shraddha_19.02.2021_D2.png\" style=\"width: 165px; height: 173px;\" /></p>\n\n<p>Hence, Z is <strong>third to the left</strong> of J.</p>",
